	(text "USB power:\n+5V is the USB VBUS supply, taken from the Raspberry Pi Pico's VBUS pin (pin 40).\nThe Pico runs from VBUS through its own VSYS diode, so VSYS is left unconnected.\n\n-5V inverter:\nU7 inverts +5V to -5V for the TMS5220 VDD.\nFC tied to V+: 150 kHz oscillator, 75 kHz charge-pump switching, above the audio band.\nLV tied to GND, OSC left open. Output is about -(VBUS - 3.5 ohm x load).\nUse low-ESR capacitors; place C16 to C20 close to U7."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 183.896 77.978 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "2c833d3d-4d13-4a37-aa26-84db70707ed2")
	)
	(text "TMS5220 supply filters:\nR29/C13/C14 (VSS) and R30/C15/C22 (VDD)\nkeep LM2662 and USB noise off the\nTMS5220 rails; fc is about 340 Hz.\nPlace C13-C15 and C22 close to U1.\nQ1 and R26 stay on the raw rails so the\nOSC switching current stays off VDD."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 84.074 142.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "330d3a05-151a-4743-b014-9ab8ddf0b8bf")
	)
	(text "OSC level shifter:\nOSC must swing between the TMS5220 rails (-5 V to +5 V).\nGPIO22 released: R25 holds Q1 off, R26 pulls OSC to -5 V. GPIO22 low: Q1 on, OSC = +5 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 177.8 157.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "b1d00251-702d-42ab-85a1-ef60bfcd41f1")
	)
